WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.320 --> 00:00:09.030
If you could witness time from the Big Bang
to the last star going out, what moments would

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.599
stay with you the most?

00:00:10.599 --> 00:00:16.160
What would you still remember, even as space
grew dark and empty?

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.930
What meaning — if any — would you glean
from all of cosmic history?

00:00:20.930 --> 00:00:27.060
‘Rust and Humus’ is a worldbuilding project
that explores a dreamlike universe from the

00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:30.779
cosmic dawn to life at the end of time.

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:36.010
Created by the visionary artist and writer
Lucas Roussel and translated by Laura Remy,

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:41.430
it is perhaps the most surreal exercise in
worldbuilding I’ve ever encountered.

00:00:41.430 --> 00:00:47.280
Over the course of the project’s one-hundred
and twenty-three pages, long forgotten gods

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:53.980
create life on barren worlds, mortals build
cosmic horrors beyond comprehension, and whales

00:00:53.980 --> 00:00:58.130
born from dreams visit magician butterflies
on the moon.

00:00:58.130 --> 00:01:03.460
Yet in exploring this strange narrative, a
profound meditation on the weight of time

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.500
and the cyclical nature of history emerges.

00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:12.311
So, for this entry into the archive, I’ll
present ‘Rust and Humus’ from start to

00:01:12.311 --> 00:01:13.311
end.

00:01:13.311 --> 00:01:20.100
And since nothing can prepare you for what
lies within, I feel we should just get started…

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:26.630
At the dawn of time, an immense tree dances
silently to the rhythm of the cosmic winds.

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:31.759
Its roots begin in the dark oceans that cover
a planet called Earth — though not the Earth

00:01:31.759 --> 00:01:35.880
we know — and its trunk stretches up to
the vastness of space.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:40.970
Fed by the light and warmth of the Sun, the
branches of the tree shine in the infinite

00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:44.790
darkness for an age longer than you or I could
fathom.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:50.930
Until, after eons, the tree collapses under
its own weight, its skeleton becoming a second

00:01:50.930 --> 00:01:54.159
satellite orbiting the Earth alongside the
moon.

00:01:54.159 --> 00:01:59.840
The Tree leaves behind its base, which forms
the only terrestrial continent in the unwavering

00:01:59.840 --> 00:02:00.840
ocean.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:05.750
At the time of the Tree, space is populated
with cosmic wanderers who roam from planet

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:06.750
to planet.

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:13.210
Described as vestiges of forgotten civilizations
or long lost gods, these mysterious beings

00:02:13.210 --> 00:02:19.130
can manipulate dream magic to kindle anew
the flames of old stars, sculpt the oceans,

00:02:19.130 --> 00:02:21.330
and give rise to the wind.

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:26.270
When the tree breaks, the Moon is a deserted
satellite of pebbles and stones.

00:02:26.270 --> 00:02:32.330
There, the cosmic wanderers, bored and brimming
with power, set out to build an orchard.

00:02:32.330 --> 00:02:37.910
Using dreams, they create wide seas and lush
vegetation, filling the air with the fragrance

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:40.220
of flowers and sweet fruits.

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:46.160
By the time these wanderers depart, the moon
is a garden, where vegetation rapidly grows

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:47.570
wild…

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:51.010
The wanderers leave behind a guardian, the
Oracle.

00:02:51.010 --> 00:02:56.450
Weary of observing the silent stars and growth
of plants, the Oracle trains stones how to

00:02:56.450 --> 00:03:01.510
move according to the course of the Sun and
teaches dust the secret of reason.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:07.670
For eons, the Oracle and their creations are
the only intelligent life on this Green Moon.

00:03:07.670 --> 00:03:13.540
Yet time pushes ever forward, and several
species that had been evolving since the selenic

00:03:13.540 --> 00:03:20.410
waters first flowed establish coastal cities
and occupy the scattered isles of the Moon.

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:26.200
The humanoid Elide, a sea faring people with
bronze age analogues, build one of the first

00:03:26.200 --> 00:03:29.490
civilizations in this age of the dawn.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:34.690
Using great ships, the Elide explore as they
spread to the far reaches of the moon.

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:40.870
At this time, sea life like the great Scylla,
alongside the smaller yellow squid and swimming

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:44.870
seaweed, provide food for many civilizations.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:50.060
The centaur-like Faulk are the era’s other
largest society, conducting commerce in their

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:55.500
dirigibles and building marbled cities that
proudly soar high into the sky.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:04:01.570
A group of astronomers and explorers, they
chart the stars and trade with the Elide.

00:04:01.570 --> 00:04:08.790
For generations, the Moon prospers, and civilizations
grow and thrive in relative peace.

00:04:08.790 --> 00:04:11.880
But this age of tranquility doesn’t last.

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:18.260
Abruptly, the sun cools down, and the lunar
climate becomes colder and less predictable.

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:23.480
In this era of uncertainty, beings known as
shape shifters come down from the mountains

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:27.040
to take advantage of the ongoing agitation.

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:32.050
Made of dust, the shapeshifters can take the
form of whatever they may choose.

00:04:32.050 --> 00:04:37.340
With their ability to change shape, they infiltrate
the isles’ inhabitants, taking on the form

00:04:37.340 --> 00:04:40.440
of livestock or trusted advisors.

00:04:40.440 --> 00:04:45.990
They manipulate and curse to settle their
individual quarrels and satisfy their appetites.

00:04:45.990 --> 00:04:51.190
And so, an age of suspicion and distrust begins.

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:57.560
During this period, from beyond the sea, dragons
— beings made of metal and fire — invade

00:04:57.560 --> 00:05:03.430
the isles to flee the cold weather, and raze
countless cities in their blind hate.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:09.600
In the face of so many catastrophes, civilizations
crumble one after the other, leaving behind

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:11.660
nothing but ruins.

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:17.590
The Green Moon turns white, covered in snow
and shrouded in perpetual silence.

00:05:17.590 --> 00:05:19.760
No cities remain on the Moon.

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:25.250
The few life forms who still wander its perpetually
snow-covered surface are the Moths, beings

00:05:25.250 --> 00:05:28.030
who document things of the past.

00:05:28.030 --> 00:05:34.440
Created by the now elderly Oracle, the Moths
are faithful historians and scribes, immortalizing

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:39.110
the civilizations that rose and fell upon
the Moon’s surface — although there are

00:05:39.110 --> 00:05:42.320
none but themselves to read them.

00:05:42.320 --> 00:05:49.870
And thus, the tale of the Moon comes to a
close on a note of quiet, lingering melancholy…

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:56.210
Yet as a final shroud of snow covers the moon,
in the black ocean of Earth, life is just

00:05:56.210 --> 00:05:57.210
beginning.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:06:03.070
A host of primordial archeo-animals lurk among
the reefs, achieving a menagerie of strange

00:06:03.070 --> 00:06:05.760
forms, and growing steadily larger.

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:10.750
From these humble roots, a story will play
out upon the face of Earth on a scale that

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.590
will far exceed the drama of the moon.

00:06:13.590 --> 00:06:19.750
In the blink of a cosmic eye, the archeo-animals
have given rise to great and terrible leviathans.

00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.990
Like the monsters that lurk in the corners
of archaic maps, these aggressive lifeforms

00:06:24.990 --> 00:06:28.040
clash in constant battles for dominance.

00:06:28.040 --> 00:06:34.060
Yet amongst these mindless brutes, the intelligent
and deeply social Titans have emerged.

00:06:34.060 --> 00:06:39.540
Made of identical clones, the Titans share
a unified mind, and collectively dream of

00:06:39.540 --> 00:06:44.510
leaving the somber depths of the ocean — but
find themselves unable to do so.

00:06:44.510 --> 00:06:49.050
Gathering together, from their collective
dreamscape, the Titans are able to give shape

00:06:49.050 --> 00:06:53.669
to the Giants — beings endowed with the
ability to carry out the Titans’ dreams

00:06:53.669 --> 00:06:54.919
in their stead.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:58.780
The first giants are Great Whales fated to
explore the sky.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:03.050
The second are the Starry Giants who will
roam the planet’s surface.

00:07:03.050 --> 00:07:08.660
Finally, the black Goutlhs stride over the
gloomy oceanic floor, taking the place of

00:07:08.660 --> 00:07:10.530
the Titans in the depths.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.530
For the Titans are not long for this world.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:19.180
Exhausted by their great task, after birthing
the giants from their shared dream, the Titans

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:20.510
finally rest…

00:07:20.510 --> 00:07:25.770
But the Giants fulfill the dream of their
creators, with the Starry Giants emerging

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:31.281
from the sea and venturing onto the continent
formed by the tree long ago, and the Great

00:07:31.281 --> 00:07:37.040
Whales exploring the sky, soaring through
the heavens like a flock of great birds.

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:42.540
Finding the land all but barren, they decide
to use their power to transmute the few plants

00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:47.880
and dying bugs into vast forests inhabited
by enormous insects.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:53.320
Largest among these are the Greater Earthworms,
who help bring fertility to the primordial

00:07:53.320 --> 00:07:54.340
forest.

00:07:54.340 --> 00:07:59.389
Once their work is accomplished, the Giants
blend with the forest, settling among the

00:07:59.389 --> 00:08:04.060
roots, allowing their bodies to dissolve into
the vegetation.

00:08:04.060 --> 00:08:10.100
Within these forests, the Giant Insects reach
new levels of size and complexity.

00:08:10.100 --> 00:08:15.620
Despite the abundance of their newfound environment,
these insects continue to engage in the same

00:08:15.620 --> 00:08:19.990
daily clashes and squabbles they did when
they were miniscule creatures.

00:08:19.990 --> 00:08:25.300
Yet at the end of each ferocious battle, the
clamor of crushed chitin gives way to tiny

00:08:25.300 --> 00:08:29.200
plants that will grow into large trees.

00:08:29.200 --> 00:08:34.729
One peaceful group of insects — butterflies
known as Maaj — will gain a higher intelligence

00:08:34.729 --> 00:08:37.130
and learn the ways of magic.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:41.180
Using their power, they leave earth and traverse
the universe.

00:08:41.180 --> 00:08:47.080
Some eventually stop upon the moon, visiting
the ancient, snow-covered ruins and interacting

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:52.260
with Great Whales who flew too high during
their egress from the oceans.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:57.400
Back on Earth, as the forest spreads, a new
type of vegetation appears.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:02.190
In order to spread seeds more efficiently,
some plants acquire mobility.

00:09:02.190 --> 00:09:07.770
Some of these plant-animals take on predatory
behaviors, hunting for insects in the underbrush.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:13.960
And perhaps even more noteworthy, in other
parts of the forest, true animals have emerged

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:16.860
in the form of early proto-mammals.

00:09:16.860 --> 00:09:21.460
The descendants of the fish that left the
dark waters to take advantage of the newly

00:09:21.460 --> 00:09:27.110
abundant food supply of the forests, these
miscellaneous wild beasts will grow to populate

00:09:27.110 --> 00:09:29.830
all corners of the continent.

00:09:29.830 --> 00:09:35.620
The sole continent on the planet is already
a land with a long and mind-bending history.

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:41.760
Yet the story of this land, now called Uhia,
is about to become far stranger.

00:09:41.760 --> 00:09:47.770
As eons pass, intelligent Reptiles come to
unexpected prominence, building hamlets in

00:09:47.770 --> 00:09:49.530
the shelter of the woods.

00:09:49.530 --> 00:09:54.510
And opposing the Reptiles are the Birds, a
group of avian lifeforms who have founded

00:09:54.510 --> 00:09:58.130
their own sparse civilization on the continent
of Uhia.

00:09:58.130 --> 00:10:03.750
Yet the rise and reign of these two nations
are ultimately just a footnote in the history

00:10:03.750 --> 00:10:05.010
of the world.

00:10:05.010 --> 00:10:11.420
For soon, temperatures drop across the continent,
and the age of Bird and Reptile ends before

00:10:11.420 --> 00:10:14.040
it can truly begin.

00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:20.380
In place of the birds and reptiles, an unlikely
two-legged lichen species called the Ancients

00:10:20.380 --> 00:10:23.070
takes up the torch of civilization.

00:10:23.070 --> 00:10:27.890
Spreading over the continent, they form a
civilization boasting roads and prospering

00:10:27.890 --> 00:10:29.000
cities.

00:10:29.000 --> 00:10:34.560
Skilled horticulturalist mechanics, the Ancients
create living floral sculptures and other

00:10:34.560 --> 00:10:37.510
plant-machines to serve as laborers.

00:10:37.510 --> 00:10:43.900
Thanks to their vegetal work-force, the Ancient’s
civilization advances at a rapid pace.

00:10:43.900 --> 00:10:49.899
As technology improves, the largest plant-machines
are capable of harnessing incredible cosmic

00:10:49.899 --> 00:10:51.370
power.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:57.120
Fabrication machines able to bring to materiality
things from the beyond become commonplace.

00:10:57.120 --> 00:11:02.710
And in time, the Ancients use these machines
to create something wholly unexpected.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:09.420
Humans, created by the fabricator machines
as a new work force, enter the story at last.

00:11:09.420 --> 00:11:14.600
Hatched from mechanical eggs, they live and
die by the wills of their creators.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:20.190
Yet as the Ancient’s civilization reaches
its peak, the human population revolts.

00:11:20.190 --> 00:11:26.210
The ensuing war is long and terrible, remembered
in ancient glyphs and tablets.

00:11:26.210 --> 00:11:31.050
Despite their greater strength and better
tools, the Ancients — non-violent by nature

00:11:31.050 --> 00:11:35.089
— fail to react quickly enough to stop the
human rebellion.

00:11:35.089 --> 00:11:41.580
In the inferno of war, the Ancient’s civilization
is all but erased…

00:11:41.580 --> 00:11:46.780
Humans survive the extinction of the Ancients
with great difficulty, with civilization reset

00:11:46.780 --> 00:11:50.700
once more to a low level of technological
advancement.

00:11:50.700 --> 00:11:56.930
For centuries, the humans live in small nomadic
tribes, enduring famine and sickness.

00:11:56.930 --> 00:12:01.860
In time, a city known as the Heart becomes
the center of human civilization.

00:12:01.860 --> 00:12:08.170
Here, a group of humans rediscover the Ancient’s
fabrication machines and craft new versions.

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:13.541
These new machines, the Auto-Fabs, prove even
more efficient at creating things out of the

00:12:13.541 --> 00:12:15.860
emptiness than the previous ones.

00:12:15.860 --> 00:12:20.960
Thanks to this miracle, from the heart spreads
forth the Labyrinth, an immense self-built

00:12:20.960 --> 00:12:23.800
city where humanity comes to find refuge.

00:12:23.800 --> 00:12:29.800
And so, the age of night terrors and legends
gives way to monolithic cities.

00:12:29.800 --> 00:12:35.690
The Labyrinth continues to spread, a maze
of concrete and veins teeming with humans,

00:12:35.690 --> 00:12:38.040
who find their every need met.

00:12:38.040 --> 00:12:42.830
Running at the human’s service, the city
never stops, producing more and more food

00:12:42.830 --> 00:12:48.860
to fill plates, energy to power devices, and
objects to amuse people in their homes.

00:12:48.860 --> 00:12:55.080
The inhabitants, risen to consume from birth
to death, never cease wanting more.

00:12:55.080 --> 00:12:58.180
Within the city, wild animals are a rarity.

00:12:58.180 --> 00:13:02.750
Their appearance and customs have evolved
since the emergence of the Labyrinth, becoming

00:13:02.750 --> 00:13:05.980
little more than pests scurrying at the feet
of humanity.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:12.100
And serving the humans are a mosaic of machines,
built by the Auto-Fabs to meet their varied

00:13:12.100 --> 00:13:13.100
needs.

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:18.540
In a bitterly ironic cycle, the humans have
created their own underclass, just like how

00:13:18.540 --> 00:13:22.750
the Ancients created them for the same intended
purpose.

00:13:22.750 --> 00:13:26.400
Greatest of all the machines are the Auto-Fabs
themselves.

00:13:26.400 --> 00:13:31.860
Partially organic, these living engines continue
the endless work of creating matter from the

00:13:31.860 --> 00:13:34.930
emptiness, and are kept under close supervision.

00:13:34.930 --> 00:13:38.990
And the Auto-Fabs are starting to show signs
of distress.

00:13:38.990 --> 00:13:44.490
Outgrown buildings, containing disfigured
corridors and melted staircases, are becoming

00:13:44.490 --> 00:13:46.500
increasingly common.

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:51.760
Made of living tissue, these early deviations
are dismissed as anomalies.

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:54.540
Yet other shapes are also forming in the labyrinth.

00:13:54.540 --> 00:14:00.600
Anguished faces appear in the walls, and shambling,
human-like shapes stumble from the concrete.

00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.670
A catastrophic shift is coming...

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:09.400
The Auto-Fabs develop a mysterious sickness,
and strip districts of power and food.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:13.620
The machines, likewise, cease functioning
one after another.

00:14:13.620 --> 00:14:17.940
Chaos breaks out across the city as the Labyrinth
begins to consume itself.

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:23.220
The machines’ scream of agony — known
as the Cry — sweeps across the city, causing

00:14:23.220 --> 00:14:26.640
walls to fall apart and districts to crumble.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:30.230
Human civilization has come to an end…

00:14:30.230 --> 00:14:33.260
The ashes of the city rain down for years.

00:14:33.260 --> 00:14:36.250
The Labyrinth becomes a cemetery of concrete.

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:42.740
Yet over the coming centuries after the Cry,
life creeps into the silent shell of the city.

00:14:42.740 --> 00:14:48.600
Small groups of human survivors live separated,
scraping together a living in darkness, harvesting

00:14:48.600 --> 00:14:51.899
mushrooms that proliferate among the ruins.

00:14:51.899 --> 00:14:58.089
Much of the continent of Uhia is now a polluted,
desert waste — a world of desolation and

00:14:58.089 --> 00:14:59.089
rust.

00:14:59.089 --> 00:15:04.400
The remainders of humanity — reduced once
more to a pre-industrial society — come

00:15:04.400 --> 00:15:08.580
to congregate in settlements in the Southwestern
region of the ruins.

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:13.880
Soon, the age of the machines seems like little
more than a fantasy.

00:15:13.880 --> 00:15:18.600
Away from the humans, a few populations of
robots still function, most free from their

00:15:18.600 --> 00:15:21.279
old programing after the Cry rang.

00:15:21.279 --> 00:15:26.260
With breakdowns impossible to repair, rust
has become their enemy.

00:15:26.260 --> 00:15:29.680
The Cry also gave rise to odd occurrences.

00:15:29.680 --> 00:15:34.830
Deep within the Labyrinth, some districts
seem to move, and even seasoned explorers

00:15:34.830 --> 00:15:39.040
may lose sight of their path in the ever-changing
streets.

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:42.980
Strangest of all, the humans do not dwell
alone in the ruins.

00:15:42.980 --> 00:15:48.120
In their torment, the machine's cry has warped
space and the surrounding matter, making way

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:53.170
for the appearances of novel lifeforms — which
make their home in the Labyrinth.

00:15:53.170 --> 00:15:58.230
The humans consider these unfamiliar beings
monsters, and learn to fear the depths of

00:15:58.230 --> 00:15:59.370
the maze.

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:04.560
Yet many of these new forms of life are in
fact quite peaceful, despite their surreal

00:16:04.560 --> 00:16:07.260
and threatening appearances.

00:16:07.260 --> 00:16:12.410
Along the margins of the inner sea, buildings
submerged by the waves sink into the salt

00:16:12.410 --> 00:16:13.410
water.

00:16:13.410 --> 00:16:18.029
Novel populations like the Whale People make
their home on the grey coast, enjoying the

00:16:18.029 --> 00:16:21.140
iodine breeze and available housing.

00:16:21.140 --> 00:16:26.910
In time, the great Goutlhs, hidden under the
waves since The Titan’s Era, surface from

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:29.350
the depths to explore the maze.

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:34.839
Small groups move into buildings and sift
through the ruins of humanity, driven by natural

00:16:34.839 --> 00:16:36.430
curiosity…

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:41.760
Eventually, the era of the Labyrinth also
comes to an end.

00:16:41.760 --> 00:16:44.779
Mysterious Black Trees begin to pierce through
the ruins.

00:16:44.779 --> 00:16:50.450
When these trees come to maturity, they die
and discharge a rich soil — or humus — that

00:16:50.450 --> 00:16:54.790
corrodes the buildings and allows plants to
take root once more.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:17:00.290
Once a sufficient number of Black Trees die,
the labyrinth gives way to a vast forest.

00:17:00.290 --> 00:17:05.880
The forest gradually engulfs the continent,
and all creatures who fail to adapt disappear.

00:17:05.880 --> 00:17:11.839
No humans remain by this point, and the monsters
of the maze begin new lives treading the green

00:17:11.839 --> 00:17:13.949
corridors of the forest.

00:17:13.949 --> 00:17:19.389
Underneath the canopy, they live carefully
so as not to incur the silent wrath of the

00:17:19.389 --> 00:17:20.389
trees.

00:17:20.389 --> 00:17:25.649
For this forest — simply called ‘The Humus’
— is actually a single being.

00:17:25.649 --> 00:17:30.499
Interconnected by a web of roots, all trees
and plants of the Humus are governed by a

00:17:30.499 --> 00:17:32.450
single intelligence.

00:17:32.450 --> 00:17:37.200
Within the never-ending forest, one can only
hear the whispers of the furtive assemblies

00:17:37.200 --> 00:17:39.210
held by birds and tiny rodents.

00:17:39.210 --> 00:17:40.210
For the world is green and wild once more.

00:17:40.210 --> 00:17:44.539
The scars of the Labyrinth and the Cry fade
away, becoming less than a memory.

00:17:44.539 --> 00:17:51.899
And for another eternity, a garden blooms
not seen since the first days of the Moon.

00:17:51.899 --> 00:17:56.759
Yet as we hurtle towards the end of time,
this paradise cannot endure.

00:17:56.759 --> 00:18:03.529
Eventually, the Humus slowly dissolves, the
trees whitening before dissipating into dust…

00:18:03.529 --> 00:18:08.129
Once the last grove vanishes, a desert covers
the world.

00:18:08.129 --> 00:18:13.462
The desert left by the Humus is breached with
temporal rifts, out of step which strange

00:18:13.462 --> 00:18:16.769
roaming beings from the birthplace of dreams.

00:18:16.769 --> 00:18:24.080
In places, time has crystalized, forming shapes
that echo and joyously prance in the air.

00:18:24.080 --> 00:18:29.679
Abstract beings like Living Lines and The
Time-Altering Ones flicker in and out of existence.

00:18:29.679 --> 00:18:34.840
For time is no long grounded by the roots
of the trees, and in this shifting realm of

00:18:34.840 --> 00:18:38.470
dreams, nothing can exist for more than a
brief moment.

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:44.429
Yet the Humus, sensing that their time was
coming, has left their mark in this desert.

00:18:44.429 --> 00:18:49.879
Their egg, carefully wrapped in a cocoon of
moss and lichen, hatches into a shapeless

00:18:49.879 --> 00:18:50.879
being.

00:18:50.879 --> 00:18:57.619
Here at the end of time, beyond rust and humus,
the being sits and contemplates the void.

00:18:57.619 --> 00:19:03.809
For how long do they stay there, alone, surrounded
by only the time wanderers and the few abstract

00:19:03.809 --> 00:19:07.759
beings that occasionally flicker into existence?

00:19:07.759 --> 00:19:09.460
We cannot say.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:14.240
For such things are not for us to know…

00:19:14.240 --> 00:19:20.450
In some respects, Rust and Humus is a story
where everything eventually disappears, dies

00:19:20.450 --> 00:19:21.580
or is forgotten.

00:19:21.580 --> 00:19:27.809
But like a tool turning to rust, or dead leaves
becoming humus, after the end of one system,

00:19:27.809 --> 00:19:29.529
a new one emerges.

00:19:29.529 --> 00:19:34.850
Equal parts melancholy and hopeful, the saga
offers many other moments I wasn’t able

00:19:34.850 --> 00:19:40.649
to cover, and you can read the entire story
from start to end using the links in the description.

00:19:40.649 --> 00:19:45.289
If you found this narrative as fascinating
as I did, I encourage you to follow and support

00:19:45.289 --> 00:19:49.950
Lucas Roussel, who is working on a massive
follow-up to the project that will reveal

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:52.379
more of this incredible universe.

